{%- comment -%}
  Renders a translation if it exists, otherwise falls back to plain text.
  Liquid's `t` filter always returns a string (even a "translation
  missing: ..." placeholder when the key isn't in locales/*.json), so
  the built-in `default` filter never actually triggers for `t`. This
  snippet does the missing-key check explicitly instead.

  Usage:
    {%- render 't-or-default', key: 'products.bundle.choose', fallback: 'Choose' -%}

  With interpolation params, pass them through `t_params` as a Liquid
  hash created via `assign ... | t: ...` is not possible through render
  params, so for parameterized strings (count, percent) this snippet
  is not used — those are handled inline in bundle-quantity-break.liquid
  with their own explicit fallback logic.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign t_value = key | t
  assign t_value_downcase = t_value | downcase
  if t_value_downcase contains 'translation missing'
    echo fallback
  else
    echo t_value
  endif
-%}
